---
kind: lore
id: gallery
title: The gallery
---

// The title screen's gallery: one entry per CG, offered once the save has
// seen it. The engine shows the picture; the entry is its caption.

<entry id="galFestival" on="gallery" title="The Lantern Festival" when="holds(cgSeen(cgFestival))">
  @narrator: A thousand paper lanterns on a black lake, and one of them is yours.
</entry>
<entry id="galRenStars" on="gallery" title="Ren — a star with your name" when="holds(cgSeen(cgRenStars))">
  @narrator: The observatory roof. Ren points at nothing in particular and says your name.
</entry>
<entry id="galMikaFinish" on="gallery" title="Mika — a tie at walking pace" when="holds(cgSeen(cgMikaFinish))">
  @narrator: Two pairs of shoes on the finish line, exactly level.
</entry>
<entry id="galSorenLetter" on="gallery" title="Soren — the letter in the stacks" when="holds(cgSeen(cgSorenLetter))">
  @narrator: A letter between two old books, in blue ink and green, dated this year.
</entry>
<entry id="galKaiDuet" on="gallery" title="Kai — the fifth bar" when="holds(cgSeen(cgKaiDuet))">
  @narrator: Four hands on a piano with a hole on either side of it.
</entry>
<entry id="galRenEnd" on="gallery" title="Ren — signed once" when="holds(cgSeen(cgRenEnd))">
  @narrator: A register with one name written in it, neatly, once.
</entry>
<entry id="galMikaEnd" on="gallery" title="Mika — services to morale" when="holds(cgSeen(cgMikaEnd))">
  @narrator: The whole hall on its feet for the slowest boy on the island.
</entry>
<entry id="galSorenEnd" on="gallery" title="Soren — on loan" when="holds(cgSeen(cgSorenEnd))">
  @narrator: A return slip, with an address on it, pinned above a desk.
</entry>
<entry id="galKaiEnd" on="gallery" title="Kai — five bars" when="holds(cgSeen(cgKaiEnd))">
  @narrator: A padlock hanging open on a piano lid, on a stage, in front of everybody.
</entry>
<entry id="galKeeperEnd" on="gallery" title="Hotaru — the new girl" when="holds(cgSeen(cgKeeperEnd))">
  @narrator: A girl in an old uniform in the front row of the ceremony, laughing, with no lantern at all.
</entry>
